<pre class=metadata>
Title: External Queries
Shortname: external-queries
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/external-queries/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification lets a style sheet ask a source outside CSS a yes-or-no question and style the
    page by the answer. A one-line '@api' rule names a web API, and a one-line '@script' rule names a
    JavaScript module, such as <code>@api --moon-phase url("https://moon.example/phase");</code>. '@param'
    rules hold the styles that apply when a named source answers true, such as
    <code>@param(--moon-phase, "full")</code>, '@error' rules hold the styles for when it can't answer, such as
    <code>@error(--moon-phase, 404)</code>, and the ''param()'' test asks the same questions from inside
    ''if()''. Answers load the way web fonts do, and a keyword after the URL chooses how, as
    '@font-face/font-display' does: by default rendering waits a short time and a later answer swaps in, while
    <code>swap</code>, <code>fallback</code>, and <code>optional</code> wait less and use late answers less.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

